{
  "slug": "artist:noel-rosa",
  "name": "Noel Rosa",
  "editorial_article": "Born in Rio de Janeiro in 1910, Noel Rosa became one of the foundational figures of Brazilian samba by transforming the genre's Afro-Brazilian roots with a witty, urban vernacular. His 1931 breakthrough hit, \"Com que roupa?\", remains a signature of his ability to weave ironic social commentary into popular song. Rosa often spent his nights in bars collaborating with figures like Vadico, with whom he co-wrote enduring tracks such as \"Conversa de botequim\" and \"Feitiço da Vila\". A member of the musical group Bando de Tangarás alongside Braguinha and Almirante, he produced roughly 250 compositions before his death from tuberculosis at age 26 in 1937. His work remains a primary influence on the development of samba canção, frequently recorded by the major voices of his era.",
